  "slug": "food",
  "title": "Food & Restaurant Color Palettes",
  "tagline": "Warm, appetizing, grounded — the palette of Japanese dining culture.",
  "description": "Japanese food culture has one of the most sophisticated visual traditions in the world: the lacquer red of a bento box lid, the earthy warmth of konbu broth, the deep amber of soy-glazed teriyaki, the yellow-gold of dashi noodles in a ceramic bowl, the burnt orange of kaki fruit at a market stall. These are the colors the eye reads as nourishing before the palate is engaged. They work for restaurant identities, food packaging, farmers market branding, cookbook design, café menus, and any project where the brief includes the phrase \"approachable and warm.\"",
